A||||9||Rodney||Carlisle: Rain and cold!!!||||1||
Z||000000||Rodney||05-21-2000||10:46 AM||||Just returned from the Carlisle Penn. show. Rained all the way there. About a 12 hour drive for me and a friend. Rained all morning. Somewhat stopped around noon. Maybe towards 1:00. I had no idea if it would star again as it was very overcast. Temps were in the lower 60's. So I did not set up my stand for any sales. My friend and I walked around and looked at cars. Ground was soaked and lots of mud. Show next year is in early Sept. That means there is a very good chance for good weather!! <P>Rodney Dickman||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||05-21-2000||01:07 PM||||Also a very good chance for snow.  Anything's possible in September in PA! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Uaana||05-21-2000||02:21 PM||||Rodney<BR>Ya shoulda come up the the MN kickoff, temps in the lower 70's, bright, sunny all weekend, little breezy but still sounds better than the carlisle meeting.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||05-21-2000||05:30 PM||||Rodney was correct about the rain.  I looked at it a free rinse water.  It cleared up enough to get the cars wiped down for judging.  It was muddy.  I'll stick a few photos from the show, then try to put together another Zing album of pictures.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DRKBlueMGTM.jpg"> <P>Miramee and Joe came down from Canada with last years "Best of Show" from FOCOA Nationals.  Nice 3.1 turbo GT..really nice<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DevilishM.jpg"> <P>PISA Corp latest Fiero Kit car.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/JalapenoM.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/JalapenointeriorM.jpg"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||jhogans||05-21-2000||06:00 PM||||I like the Fieros.<P>What kind of side scoops are those on the blue Fiero?  I really like those.<P>What kind of rims are on the black Fiero?  Do they come in Red?<P>I really like that kit.  I didn't realize it was a Fiero until I saw the interior.  Do you have any more photos of this kit.  I wouldn't mind dropping this kit on a beat up Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||CUTTER||05-21-2000||08:04 PM||||Hey, do you have a picture of the blue zr2 that was beside of the jalapeno? That was one of the nicest fieros there! Thats what i want to do to my 87GT. Also, get a picture of the fiero with the corvette motor?||||reg||1
Z||000006||deceler8||05-21-2000||09:43 PM||||Hey Rodney...I'll guarantee hot and humid when you're in Onawa, Iowa in July.<P>Prior to this past week I might have guaranteed dry weather too.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Sillhouette.com||05-21-2000||11:19 PM||||Yep there is the coffe table built by Race Tech.  I know a lot about that car.  I got the pistons for it and know that the turbo was and probably is not working to this day.  That is the car that runs 16s in the 1/4 mile and had the turbo pipings crack all the time.  That is the  car that turned me from turbo fieros.  Also the fact that Joe F##ked up my tranny does not help.  The guy that owned my fiero before took it to him to have the Monzie serviced ended up with a Z24 transmission that I had to change back to the original tranny a year latter.  The tranny that was originally in my fiero was taken apart (by Joe) and parts were missing enverywhere.  For a tranny rebuild that usually costs 600 dollars I paied 1200 dollars.  So here is the lesson don't take anything to those butchers aka. Race Tech ever learn from my misfortune.  <P>Thanks for letting me vent <P>Later.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Old Lar||05-22-2000||12:09 AM||||Try <A HREF="http://www.zing.com/album/?id=4294350153" TARGET=_blank>http://www.zing.com/album/?id=4294350153</A> <P>or <A HREF="http://www.zing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.zing.com</A>  click on "MY ZING"<P>Type a search on FIERO, then GO  Other fiero zing albums appear.<P>I didn't get a photo of Hank's ZR1.  He wants to sell it make him an offer.  It has a 3.1 V6.<P>I didn't get a shot of Joes Corvette powered Fiero.  I'll did through my files.  I have photos from years in the past.<P>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 05-22-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 05-22-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000009||superXmotorsports||05-23-2000||11:28 AM||||Yeah the weather was a little rough!  Nice meeting some of you at the show:  Cobra427, Phil, and Pretender.  I didn't see you Cutter or was I just in hypothermia?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Too bad Dan (PISA) didn't have the yellow gauges installed in the Jalepeno for the pic!  Unfortunately I didn't get to see any of the Fiero show or the rest of the grounds due to lack of help at my spot, so I look forward to more pictures.<P>SXM||||reg||1
